    "created_at": "2025-11-06T12:18:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-11-06T12:19:52Z",
    "body": "Not throwing means unreliable API and in order for the caller to know if the method call succeeded or not, one needs to always check what value is stored in history.state after replace/pushState call. That seems rather weird and error prone API.\nTwo implementations already throw and we've seen very few issues with the throwing behavior, and would see less if all the implementations followed the current spec.\n\nThe following will start logging false in Chrome after 200. That is just very surprising logic. Caller thinks we're in some state Y, when we actually are still in X.\ndata:text/html,<html><head><script>function test() {for (let i = 0; i < 1000; ++i) {history.replaceState(i, null);console.log(history.state == i);}}</script></head><body onload=\"setTimeout(test)\"></body></html>",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
